SUMMARY:Spring Wildflower Walk at Penny's Bend
DESCRIPTION:with Ed Harrison\, Naturalist \nThis hike will provide a wonderful opportunity to see rare flora at Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve\, owned by the Army Corps of Engineers\, and managed by the North Carolina Botanical Garden. Baptisia aberrans is an imperiled species at the state level and survives in only a small number of remnant Piedmont prairie or savanna patches. The Garden’s management practices at Penny’s Bend has favored a variety of prairie and savanna flora. \nAbout 2 miles in length\, much of this hike is on primitive trails over uneven terrain\, with one short\, steep climb up from the river. Wear sturdy hiking footwear and bring insect repellent\, water\, and a walking stick\, if you ever use one. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/spring-wildflower-walk-at-pennys-bend/
LOCATION:Penny’s Bend Nature Preserve\, Old Oxford Rd\, Durham\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hikes and Tours
GEO:36.0860873;-78.8475216
